## an8.119
an8.119:1.1 | S: “For insight into greed, eight things should be developed. | T: “Bhikkhus, for direct knowledge of lust, eight things are to be developed.
an8.119:1.2 | S: What eight? | T: What eight?
an8.119:1.3 | S: Perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, limited, both pretty and ugly. | T: (1) One percipient of forms internally sees forms externally, limited, beautiful or ugly.
an8.119:1.4 | S: Mastering them, they perceive: ‘I know and see.’ | T: Having overcome them, he is percipient thus: ‘I know, I see.’
an8.119:1.5 | S: Perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, limitless, both pretty and ugly. … | T: (2) One percipient of forms internally sees forms externally, measureless, beautiful or ugly. Having overcome them, he is percipient thus: ‘I know, I see.’
an8.119:1.6 | S: Not perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, limited, both pretty and ugly. … | T: (3) One not percipient of forms internally sees forms externally, limited, beautiful or ugly. Having overcome them, he is percipient thus: ‘I know, I see.’
an8.119:1.7 | S: Not perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, limitless, both pretty and ugly. … | T: (4) One not percipient of forms internally sees forms externally, measureless, beautiful or ugly. Having overcome them, he is percipient thus: ‘I know, I see.’
an8.119:1.8 | S: Not perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, blue, with blue color and blue appearance. … | T: (5) One not percipient of forms internally sees forms externally, blue ones, blue in color, with a blue hue, with a blue tint …
an8.119:1.9 | S: yellow … | T: (6) … yellow ones, yellow in color, with a yellow hue, with a yellow tint …
an8.119:1.10 | S: red … | T: (7) … red ones, red in color, with a red hue, with a red tint …
an8.119:1.11 | S: Not perceiving form internally, they see forms externally, white, with white color and white appearance. | T: (8) … white ones, white in color, with a white hue, with a white tint.
an8.119:1.12 | S: Mastering them, they perceive: ‘I know and see.’ | T: Having overcome them, he is percipient thus: ‘I know, I see.’
an8.119:1.13 | S: For insight into greed, these eight things should be developed.” | T: For direct knowledge of lust, these eight things are to be developed.”

## an8.11
an8.11:1.1 | S: So I have heard. | T: Thus have I heard.
an8.11:1.2 | S: At one time the Buddha was staying in Verañjā at the root of a neem tree dedicated to Naḷeru. | T: On one occasion the Blessed One was dwelling at Verañjā at the foot of Naḷeru’s neem tree.
